    "code": "def solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    advertising_expenditure = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\n    monthly_sales_revenue = [15, 30, 50, 40, 65]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    n = len(advertising_expenditure)\n    sum_x = sum(advertising_expenditure)\n    sum_y = sum(monthly_sales_revenue)\n    sum_x_squared = sum(x ** 2 for x in advertising_expenditure)\n    sum_xy = sum(\n        x * y\n        for x, y in zip(advertising_expenditure, monthly_sales_revenue)\n    )\n\n    slope = (\n        (n * sum_xy - sum_x * sum_y)\n        / (n * sum_x_squared - sum_x ** 2)\n    )\n    answer = f\"{slope:.2f}\"\n\n    # return answer\n    return answer\n"
